{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-resolvent","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-resolvent","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Resolvent (categorical)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential"],"tags":["resolvent","q-laplacian","spectral","hopf-algebra"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QResolvent","text":"q-resolvent.md","leanSource":"q-resolvent.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-resolvent\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widehat{\\Delta_q}</code> be the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian acting on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s \\in \\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathbf{C}}(\\mathbf{1}, A)</code> be a categorical spectral parameter. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-resolvent</strong> is the morphism</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  R_q(s) \\;=\\; \\bigl(s + \\widehat{\\Delta_q}\\bigr)^{-1} \\;\\in\\; \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A),</code></pre>\n<p>defined wherever <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s + \\widehat{\\Delta_q}</code> is invertible in the convolution algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.22.1","page":"b/def-q-resolvent","qa":{"counts":{"pass":79,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":56},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QResolvent","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent.lean","compiles":"unchecked","